1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''FYI:''' "Podunk" was not a town. It was and is the name of a tributary river running from the southeast through South Windsor through a bit of East Hartford into the Connecticut River. Hence, lands through which
2 CONC  the Podunk ran were generally named Podunk lands. — (CT resident: Ken Shelley, 2 Jan 2026)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He died after his Will and before the Inventory date.''' Any attempt to declare a specific date of death one might see is not supported by a primary source.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Wikitree: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Burnham-405 John Burnham (abt. 1649–1721)]
2 CONT Last modified 27 Jun 2020
2 CONT
2 CONT >Some secondary sources list, as John's wife, Mary CATLIN, while others list Mary OLCOTT. — The author of source 2 (below) states Mary Catlin was John's wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Burnham, son of Thomas born about 1652 East Hartford. Birth date is estimated from Winthrop's Medical Records.[4]. He married 12 Nov 1668, to Mary Catlin ??, born 10 Jul 1666, daughter of John Catlin and Mary Marshall.
2 CONT
2 CONT John owned covenant with First Church 26 Oct 1686. John was a large landholder. There is a deed from Thomas Burnham Sr., to his son John of lands at Podunk. There is also a deed from Popo, a native american, to John Burnham of lan
2 CONC ds on the Connecticut River. Page 80-1-4 Name: John Burnham Location: Hartford
2 CONT
2 CONT John Burnham, son of Thomas married Nov 12, 1684 to Mary OLCOTT ???
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary admitted full communicant First Church May 1672
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Mary raised their 10 children on his inherited portion of his fathers estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Thomas Burnham, baptized 26 Dec 1686 in Hartford, d. 1705.
2 CONT # Caleb Burnham b. ''circa'' 1688 m 20 Mar 1735 Sarah --- (Gaylord ?)
2 CONT # John Burnham bap. 24 Oct 1689 marr 17 Oct 1720 Sarah SPENCER.
2 CONT # Mary Burnham, baptized 19 Dec 1690. She married 6 Jun 1717 to Stephen Webster
2 CONT # Rachel Burnham, baptized 30 Mar 1692
2 CONT # Amy Burnham, baptized 30 Jul 1693 in Hartford
2 CONT # Sarah Burnham, baptized 15 Sep 1695 in Hartford, d. 11 May 1767 She married 7 Dec 1727 to Elisha Pratt
2 CONT # Elizabeth Burnham, baptized 28 Feb 1696/7 in Hartford
2 CONT # Jonathan Burnham, baptized 26 Feb 1696/97, d. 17 Feb 1787 in Buckland, CT, Buckland is a part of Manchester, CT. Jonathan married 12 Nov 1727 to Hannah Bidwell
2 CONT # Jabez Burnham, baptized 14 May 1699 in Hartford, d. 27 Jul 1758. Jabez married 12 Jul 1725 to Martha Williams
2 CONT # John died 20 Apr 1721 in Podunk, Sooth Windsor, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===="Last Will and Testament of John Burnham Late of Hartford"[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Invt. £487-18-07. Taken 15 May 1721 by Samuel Burnham and Jabez Colt. Will dated 12th April, 1721.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT I, John Burnham, do make and ordain this my last will and testament: I give to my loving wife 1-3 part of all my houseing and land; also 1-3 part of all personal estate to be at her own dispose.
2 CONT
2 CONT I give my son John Burnham 10 acres of meadow land, being part of my lower lott, he to have it on the south side of sd. lott as is abutted southerly on land of Samuel Burnham and Richard Gilman, the east end to be at the upland, t
2 CONC he west end at Podunk River, the north side to be a straight line from the upland to Podunk River. Also, I give to my son John 17 acres of upland on the east side of the country road which lies westward of sd. son's now dwelling h
2 CONC ouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT I give unto my three sons, Jonathan Burnham, Jabez Burnham and Caleb Burnham, all the rest of my meadow land and swamp land in Podunk Meadow (not given to my son John) to be equally divided between them. As to the number of acres,
2 CONC  my sons Jonathan and Jabez to have my upper lott, my son Caleb to have his part next to and abutting upon the 10 acres of meadow given my son John. The remainder of my lower lott to be equally divided between my sd. sons Jonathan
2 CONC  and Jabez.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, I give to son Jonathan 1-2 of my piece of land lying westward of the lane or way that runs westward of my dwelling house to John Morton's house, my sd. son to have the north half of sd. piece of land; and also I give sd. Jon
2 CONC athan 1-4 part of all my land which lyeth eastward of the 17 acres of upland given to my son John.
2 CONT Also, I give to my son Jabez 1-2 of my dwelling house.
2 CONT
2 CONT I give unto my son Caleb 1-2 of my piece of land lying westward of the before mentioned lane or way to John Morton's house; also the easterly part of my orchard. Also I give my son Caleb the other half of my dwelling house and the
2 CONC  land it standeth on, for and during the term of 10 years after he come to the age of 21 years, and at the end of that time the sd. half of my house to belong to my son Jabez.
2 CONT
2 CONT I give unto my daughter Mary Webster ?10.
2 CONT
2 CONT I give unto my 4 daughters, Rachell, Amy, Sarah and Elizabeth, all the rest of my moveables or personal estate not before in this my will disposed of, to be equally divided between them. But my will is that if the sd. estate given
2 CONC  to my 4 daughters shall or do not amount to the value of ?35 as money at the inventory price for each of my sd. 4 daughters, that then my 4 sons, John, Jonathan, Jabez and Caleb, shall pay unto each of my sd. 4 daughters so much 
2 CONC as will make up each of their portions to the sum of ?35 as money, to be recovered of them or either of them my sd. sons as shall neglect or refuse to pay his part of the same to my sd. daughters or either of them within one year 
2 CONC after their portions become due to them.
2 CONT
2 CONT I make my wife Mary executrix, and my son John Burnham executor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witness: William Pitkin, Samuel Burnham, John Morton.
2 CONT John Burnham, ls.
2 CONT Court Record, Page 150 2 May, 1721 Will proven [sic; not proved before inventory; original document at Ancestry does not show a probate date.]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Connecticut, U.S., Wills and Probate Records, 1609-1999: Hartford District. Probate Records, Vol 9-10, 1716-1729. [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/9049/images/007627225_00052?pId=321920 Ancestry.com].
2 CONT # Manwaring, Charles William, ed. ''A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records''. Vol. 2, p. 365. [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=uva.x000856596&view=1up&seq=377&size=150&q1=12th+April,+1721 Babel.HathiTrust]
2 CONT # Burnham, Roderick Henry. ''Genealogical Records of Thomas Burnham, The Emigrant'' (Case, Lockwood & Brainard Co., Hartford, Conn., 1884) [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalreco00inburn/page/n146/mode/1up page 121], [https:
2 CONC //archive.org/details/genealogicalreco00inburn/page/125/mode/1up page 125]: footnote explains Mary Catlin is the correct wife.
2 CONT # ''Winthrop Family Papers Dates: 1537-1990'' Bulk Dates: 1620-1900 Physical Description: 62 document boxes, 121 volumes, 5 extra-tall volumes, and 6 oversize boxes Call Number: Ms. N-262; Ms. N-263 (photostats) Microfilm Call Num
2 CONC ber: P-350, 53 reels Repository: Massachusetts Historical Society 1154 Boylston Street Boston, MA 02215
