2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Samuel2 Burnham, (Thomas1) b. 1650, d. 12 Apr 1738, resided in East Windsor, Hartford, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT A man of property, he gave each of his sons a home and a farm.
2 CONT Recorded in Vol. XII, Page 139 Name: Samuel Burnham, Sen. Location: Hartford
2 CONT Died 19 April, 1728. Invt. ?735-04-11. Taken 6 May, 1728, by Gabriel Williams and John Wood. Will dated 20 November, 1727.
2 CONT I give to my wife Mary Burnham all the household stuff, goods and estate whatsoever yt she brought with her at the time of her marriage with me, and also one pide cow, to be at her own dispose forever. I give to my son Samuel Burn
2 CONC ham the house in which he dwells and the land on which it stands, bounded west on a highway, south on land of John Burnham, north on land of John Woods, the bredth of my lott (excepting two rods on the north side extending eastwa
2 CONC rd within 8 rods of the house, hereafter given to my son Joseph Burnham). I give to my son Joseph Burnham his house and 14 acres of land. I give to my son William Burnham the house in which he dwells, with land bounded west on lan
2 CONC d of heirs of Thomas Burnham, Jr., decd., south on Jonah Williams, north on Charles Burnham. I give to my sons Daniel and Timothy Burnham, equally to be divided between them, my dwelling house, barn and homelott. I give to my daug
2 CONC hter Hannah Drake, to my daughter Ann Trumble, and to her eldest son  Trumble, to my daughter Mary Church, and to my daughter Rebeckah Burnham. I appoint my sons Samuel Burnham and Joseph Burnham to be executors.
2 CONT Witness: Jonathan Burnham, Jabez Burnham, William Pitkin.
2 CONT Samuel Burnham, ls.
2 CONT Court Record, Page 193May, 1728: Will proven.
2 CONT A DIGEST OF THE EARLY CONNECTICUT PROBATE RECORDS.
2 CONT 1723 to 1729.
2 CONT He married Mary Cadwell, married 8 Oct 1684, b. 8 Jan 1659, d. 19 Apr 1738.
2 CONT Mary: Daughter of Thomas Cadwell and Elizabeth Stebbins Wilson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT Hannah3 Burnham b. 1686.
2 CONT Rebecca Burnham, b. 1688, baptized 5 Dec 1688, d. post 1728. Never married.
2 CONT Anna Burnham, b. 1690, baptized 10 Oct 1690, d. 10 Aug 1753. Married Ammis Trumbull on May 8,1711.
2 CONT Mary Burnham, b. 1692, baptized 13 Mar 1692, d. 10 Mar 1767.Married John Church on Dec. 4,1722.
2 CONT Samuel Burnham, b. 1694, baptized 11 Feb 1694, d. unmarried.
2 CONT Joseph Burnham b. 1696.
2 CONT William Burnham b. 20 Jul 1698.
2 CONT David (LT.) Burnham, b. 1700, baptized 26 Mar 1700, resided in Hartford, Hartford, CT. Fathers will says Daniel not David.He married Damaris Spencer.
2 CONT Timothy Burnham b. 1705.
2 CONT Marriage 8 Oct 1684. Hartford, Hartford, Connecticut, United States.
2 CONT
