1 NOTE Graduated at Yale 1709.  He was first mentioned in the colonial  records May 20, 1714, when at a meeting of the "Governour" and Council in Hartford, "Mr. Nathaniel Burnham is appointed Surveyor to attend our Commissioners in runni
2 CONC ng the line between this Colony and the Massachusett Province."  Became Deputy from Wethersfield 1722, and he continued to be Deputy for the years through 1725 and again elected Deputy 1732 & 1733.
