1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''~• It seems to have been WIlliam who was the primary force that moved his family from Tolland CT to the wilds of Thetford, Orange Co., VT. others, like his son Thomas came along with a wife [https://www.geni.com/
2 CONC people/Mabel-Burnham/6000000213240411824 Mabel née Sexton.] Another son, William III,,  was was a known congregant of the First Congragetional. William iii's wife [https://www.geni.com/people/Mehitable-Burnham/6000000213316936825 
2 CONC Mehitable] is in church records.''
2 CONT
2 CONT ''~• " The Burnham genealogy by Roderick H. Burnham is not clear about this line" < form notes  at the Thetford Hist. Soc. ; retrieved Jan, 2025 {MMvB}
2 CONT
2 CONT ==sources==
2 CONT for William and his immediate descendants check
2 CONT * https://researchworks.oclc.org/archivegrid/collection/data/781296226
2 CONT ** First Congregational Church of Thetford records, 1773-2004
2 CONT First Congregational Church (Thetford, Vt.).
2 CONT ** 24 boxes
2 CONT Early church records (1791-1840), many compiled by '''''Asa Burton; papers (1818-1830) of Asa Burton,''''' †† including early church history and notes written by Mary B. Slade; confessions, complaints, trials (1787-1899); treasure
2 CONC r's receipts and records (1788-1981); trustees' reports; annual reports; by-laws; personal records (1933-1945) of Rev. William Estabrook; letters and sermons of Rev. Edward Jackson Tyler (1960-1967); bulletins (1945-1979); organiz
2 CONC ation and committee records; materials relating to the United Church of Christ; and other records
2 CONT The Town of Thetford, Vt., was created by charter in 1761 and in 1773 it voted to provide for a minister, the Rev. Clement Sumner, when 11 members "laid in the foundation of the church." In 1778, Asa Burton became pastor and remai
2 CONC ned for over 50 years. In 1781 a log cabin was built to serve the congregation but by 1787 a more permanent building was erected on what is now the village common. This was moved in 1830 on wooden rollers to its present location a
2 CONC nd has been renovated over the years. In 1953 a major addition included Sunday School rooms, kitchen, office, and gathering room. In 2004 a further addition brought the building into compliance with federal acessibility and safety
2 CONC  regulations. It is believed to be the "oldest church in continuous use in the State of Vermont." It merged with UCC in 1960
2 CONT The material described in this catalog record is located in the collections of the Thetford Historical Society, Thetford, Vt
2 CONT Collection open for research
2 CONT * The First Congregational Church, Thetford, Vermont, 1937; Slade, William, 1856-1948; Brooks Memorial Library
2 CONT ** Details
2 CONT 28 p. : ill., port. ; 23 cm
2 CONT Historical material about the First Congregational Church, Thetford, Vt. (founded 1773) furnished by Rev. and Mrs. William Slade. Cover design by Philip Martin
2 CONT The material described in this catalog record is located in the collections of the Brooks Memorial Library, Brattleboro, Vt
2 CONT Cover title
2 CONT Collection open for research
2 CONT
2 CONT * 3rd item: [https://researchworks.oclc.org/archivegrid/collection/data/237644921 Child family papers, 1775-1940]
2 CONT ** Genealogical records, correspondence, legal and business papers; diaries and account books. Legal papers of Bela Child as Justice of the Peace, Thetford, Vt. Record of an ecclesiastical council of First Congregational Church, T
2 CONC hetford. Correspondence with Boston and Maine Railroad and with Justin Morrill, relating to timber rights; letters on pioneer life and missionary work in the mid-west from Mary E. Ainslie, and others. Materials on Eclipse Grange, 
2 CONC Thetford, Vt
2 CONT *** Holographs, some signed; printed forms completed in ms.; printed matter
2 CONT Unpublished guide in the repository in the Dartmouth College - Rauner Special Collections Library
2 CONT
2 CONT †† more on Asa Burton in the Rauner Library in Hanover
2 CONT [https://researchworks.oclc.org/archivegrid/collection/data/237360351 Sermons, 1777-1822] (Copies of his sermons delivered in Thetford, Vt)
2 CONT Burton, Asa, 1752-1836
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Asa Burton & Thetford==
2 CONT See: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asa_Burton
2 CONT "Asa Burton (August 25, 1752 – May 1, 1836)"
2 CONT ''ordained as a minister on January 19, 1779.[ For most of his career, Burton's ministry was in Thetford''
2 CONT
