1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for NEW YORK.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A090034  DAR Ancestor # A090034]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/35955420/charles-phelps
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT (f/g) Charles "Charley" Phelps Birth: 	Aug. 16, 1717 Northampton Hampshire County Massachusetts, USA Death: 	Apr. 17, 1789 Marlboro Windham County Vermont, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Abigail Burnham and Nathaniel Phelps III.
2 CONT
2 CONT An attorney, who had practiced in Massachusetts and New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (1) Dorothy King Root, 24 April 1740 at Hadley, Hampshire County, Massachusetts. They had two sons, Solomon and Timothy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Removed to the territory during the 1760's and on the third attempt to charter the settlement of the township of Marlboro, Phelps and his associates were successful.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles, as the principal grantee, was directed to call town meetings in accordance with the granted Charter. The town was laid out in May 1762.
2 CONT
2 CONT Among the first settlers, he and his family took up a farm in April 1764. They were confirmed Torys and although bearing a prominent part in the history of the town, Charles was persecuted on account of his devotion and allegiance
2 CONC  to New York, his former state.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was fined, imprisoned, lost property and suffered banishment because of his defiance of local government policies.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married (2) Esther Kneeland sometime after his first wife's death in 1778.
2 CONT
2 CONT Considered eccentric by town folks, his family was unhappy and his older son died tragically the year after Charles passed away. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Dorothy King Root Phelps (1715 - 1777)
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Solomon Phelps (1741 - 1790)*
2 CONT   Timothy Sr. Phelps (1747 - 1817)
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Phelps Cemetery Marlboro Windham County Vermont, USA Plot: #5  Created by: history4sure Record added: Apr 16, 2009 Find A Grave Memorial# 35955420
