2 CONT
2 CONT Reuben Webster was a storekeeper and active in local affairs. He served in the American Revolutionary War and was a jailer in the late 1790s; constable, 1805; selectman, 1822-1824; grand juror, 1824; and assessor, 1828. He married
2 CONC  Ann Buell (1781-1841) and they had four children. Ref.< https://archives.litchfieldhistoricalsociety.org/repositories/2/resources/280/collection_organization >
