1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''John had a passion for buying and selling. When I was a boy it was said that "John Hayden once owned all the land from the Ebby Hayden corner to the river." He built five houses west of his father's, kept store a
2 CONC nd lived in them one by one, his family remaining in the last one built until about 1840. He was not successful in business and died leaving a small estate. His widow died in extreme old age. When I commenced this genealogical hun
2 CONC t, she rendered me valuable assistance. Her grandfather, Ammi Trumble, was a brother of Joseph Trumbull, the father of "Brother Jonathan."'' -- Jabez Haskell Hayden.  [http://www.holcombegenealogy.com/data/p990.htm (ref. here)]
