1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "family says that he came to VT first to clear land with his father'' in THS files
2 CONT
2 CONT at some time before Sep. 13, 1796, Thomas'  1st wife Mabel eloped. see <timeline>
2 CONT
2 CONT There are hints that Mabel returned to the relationship to bear two additional children before leaving (or dying?)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==The 1800 Census of Thetford==
2 CONT List a "Caleb Burnham" living next to other in the extensive group of Thetford Burnhams. The ages would match
2 CONT Thomas, Mabel and their children.. Perhaps Thomas' nickname or middle name was Caleb as there are no other records for any Caleb in that dfamily
2 CONT
2 CONT Betsey Burnham 1806–  & Stilman Burnham 1809–1856 are said to have been these two children
2 CONT Perhaps Betsey and Stillman Burnham were Ruth's children... ??
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT in Census lists a Thomes Burnham shows
2 CONT 1790 :in Thetford
2 CONT 1800 (not found
2 CONT 1810 in Thetford
2 CONT 1820 in Thetford
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT grave stone is shard w/ his last wife Ruth: https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/199563222/ruth_burnham
