1 NOTE {geni:about_me} George Alexander McKnight Born: 1738, Rowan, North Carolina  Marriage: Catherine Lee in 1762 in North Carolina  Died: Feb 1, 1791, Surry, North Carolina  Noted events in his life were: • Biography. 2 First Settlers
2 CONC  in the Clemmons Area by Ann Ellis Sheek written for the Courier, June 19, 1975
2 CONT
2 CONT George McKnight, an industrious Scot-Irish emigrant, became the next recorded resident in this section when he purchased 611 acres of land and registered it August 27, 1762.
2 CONT
2 CONT Although visited by the Moravian Brethren from Salem, McKnight and his son Alexander were instrumental in establishing Methodism in Clemmons. His home was available as a preaching place for any demonination that requested it to ho
2 CONC ld religious services. Evidently the most requests came from the Methodists and by 1790 Clemmons was the center of Methodism in western North Carolina. Methodist Church history documents this McKnight's congregation as having been
2 CONC  organized in 1780. The first annual Methodist Conference was held in Clemmons in 1789 at McKnight's Meeting House.
2 CONT
2 CONT This Meeting House was located just west of the village on Clemmons on the knoll to the right of the roadside park at the intersection of Lasater Lake Road and Highway 158.
2 CONT
2 CONT Methodists from as far away as Kentucky travelled by horseback and on foot to attend this historic conference and later ones which were also held at McKnight's.
2 CONT
2 CONT An old camp meeting ground was here on McKnight's property in the Moravian records, the Brethren wrote about these camp meetings and appeared concerned that the Moravian young people were much attracted to these gatherings.
2 CONT
2 CONT Since all the neighboring people probably came for miles around to camp and attend these meetings, evidently these meetings were among the main social activities of that time in the history of Clemmons.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.fmoran.com/clemmons.html
2 CONT * Updated from [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=82935908 Find A Grave Memorial] via daughter [http://www.geni.com/profile-34674935887 Jane  Johnson (born McKnight)] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartC
2 CONC opy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 20 2015, 10:37:44 UTC''
2 CONT
