2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT     7 Nov 1741
2 CONT     Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT Death
2 CONT     19 Feb 1824 (aged 82)
2 CONT     Hartford, Washington County, New York, USA
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT     Old Hartford Cemetery
2 CONT     Hartford, Washington County, New York
2 CONT
2 CONT Asahel was born in Hartford, Connecticut, son of Asahel and Damaris (Gilman) Hodge. He was a Captain in the Army during the Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married three times. First to Thankful Potter. They lived in Connecticut and had at least six children. They moved to Hartford, NY and Thankful died in 1796. Capt. Asahel then married Elizabeth Brown. She passed away in 179
2 CONC 9. They did not have any children. Finally, he married Sarah Slocum. They lived in Saratoga, NY. It is unsure whether they had children or not. Asahel died in 1824 in Saratoga, but is buried in the family plot in Hartford, NY. His
2 CONC  third wife, Sarah, remarried to a Mr. Wilson, and is buried elsewhere.
