1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Glastonbury, CT.  Settled in  Amenia, Dutchess, NY.  He resided at the old Wheeler's place in 1780.  The family was in Wyoming at the time of massacure, where both his father and brother were killed.  Asa Holl
2 CONC ister escaped.
2 CONT
2 CONT Three children: Rev. Allen Hollister, Asa Hollister Jr and Timothy Hollister
2 CONT
2 CONT - Early History of Amenia, 1875, Newton Reed page 95. A Revolutionary Soldier
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother's name Luretia, surname and burial location unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT {Thank you Robert for information about his mother.}* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/30388139/asa-hollister Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 6 2019, 19:04:5
2 CONC 1 UTC''
