2 CONT
2 CONT 168 ELIJAH (David 45 Michael 1) 
2 CONT b. 20 May 1719 New Milford, CT 
2 CONT m. 25 Apr 1754 Tyrlngham, MA,   Abigail Thomas daughter of Ephraim Thomas 
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN 
2 CONT #607A Eunice b. 2 Feb. 1755 Tyrlngham, MA d. 21 Oct. 1815 age 62 buried Riverside Cem. Chemung, NY  m. Abraham Brewer d. 17 May 1814 [tombstone says 1811] buried. Riverside Cem. age 70 years, 1 month, 2 days 
2 CONT #607B Anne b. 2 Apr 1756  d. 17 Mar. 1763/4 Tyrlngham, MA 
2 CONT #607C David b. 13 Mar 1761 
2 CONT #607D Gideon b. 12 May 1763 Tyringham, MA d. 26 Feb 1806, age 44  m. Mary Mallory d. 19 May 1810 age 43 buried Riverside Cemetery, Elmira, NY 
2 CONT #607E Sybil baptised Mar. 1765 
2 CONT #608F Elijah b. 1767 
2 CONT #607G Patience 
2 CONT #607H Elisha b. 23 Dec 1774 baptised 27 Apr 1775
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT According to recent DAR findings, Elijah did not serve in the Revolution, so shouldn't be listed here. Elijah does NOT have a marker in the cemetery, but according to CT records he was born in Farmington 10 May 1719 and according 
2 CONC to the cemetery records he died after 1818.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
