1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/60200540/henry-richardson
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in the Piscataquis (ME) Observer 7 Apr 1881 p2: "Rev. Henry Richardson, a Congregational minister, died in Gilead, Maine, March 14th [discrepancy], aged 82 years. Mr. Richardson was a native of Springfield, Massachusetts
2 CONC , and graduated from Bangor Seminary in 1830. He was ordained at Sidney, Maine, in 1831, remaining two years pastor. He went to Brownville and was installed pastor in 1834, supplying that church, Williamsburg and Milo until 1838. 
2 CONC From thence, he went to Gilead, Maine, supplying that church and Shelburne, New Hampshire, and of which he was installed joint pastor in 1840. In 1849 he was at Sebasticook, Sidney and Vassalboro, and then was called to Goshen, Ne
2 CONC w Hampshire, where he remained until 1861, when he returned to Gilead. Here he has remained since that time, suffering for about twenty years from rheumatic troubles, which rendered him unable to walk or stand. He has been a dilig
2 CONC ent and faithful minister and pastor."
