1 NAME Solomon /Merrill/
2 GIVN Solomon
2 _MARNM Merrill
2 NICK Solomon Merrell
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 4 SEP 1814
2 ADDR
3 STAE ON
3 CTRY Canada
1 DEAT
2 DATE 22 OCT 1896
2 ADDR
3 CITY Roseneath
3 STAE ON
3 CTRY Canada
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Merrill, the Subject of this brief sketch was born in the township of Percy, Sept. 4th 18.14. He was the youngest son of Roger and Chloe Merrill, who were among the first settlers of the above township. He was conv
2 CONC erted to God in 1837 and at once united with the M. E. Church on the Brighton Circuit.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1841. he was married to Anna Maria Lapp, daughter of Samuel and Catherine Lapp, of the township of Haldimand. Three years after their marriage they moved to the township Alnwick where they settled on a farm, and by diligence se
2 CONC cured a beautiful home. In 1845, the Rev.Wm.Bird visited this settlement and took up an appointment in Father Merrill's house, formed a class and appointed him leader, an office which he has held ever since.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1857 he gave a lot upon which a church was built; and also rendering material assistance in the erection of the church.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held an Exhorter's license and was called upon to attend many funerals.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a constant reader of the Advocate since it was first published in Cobourg, and after the Union the Guardian has been a weekly visitor to his home. Four daughters were born to them to cheer and gladden their hearts. His fait
2 CONC hful and devoted companion has preceded him to the home above.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a man of simple, earnest faith, a devoted Christian and enjoyed the confidence of all of his neighbors. He was kind and true and the faithful friend of the Methodist ministers. As the end drew near his trust in the loving S
2 CONC avior became more evident. He peacefully passed away to his home above on the 22nd of October, 1896.
2 CONT
2 CONT Another note gives this testimony of Solomon Merrill:
2 CONT
2 CONT He was one of the pioneers in Alnwick Township near Roseneath village. He helped to carve a civilization out of a wilderness. He cleared the land of heavy timber, through the rocks in the fence corners, broke ground and made their
2 CONC  farm. He built and lived in log houses until he could build better. They were self- reliant because God guided.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have heard him conduct services in the little church when the preacher was absent. He held an exhorter's license from the Methodist Episcopal Church Conference issued to him yearly.
2 CONT
2 CONT In September 26, 1881, I was at grandfathers and asked to have him write in my autograph album. He leaned back in his chair, closed his eyes, sat for some time, then told grandmother to write in my book:'' "Where ever you stray do
2 CONC n't forget that you must pray, and when the storms of life is ore, I hope we will meet on Canans shore"'' -- She wrote it for him and also on the opposite page put her autograph.
2 CONT
2 CONT A letter from Charlton S. Grigg, Secretary Treasurer of the Merrill Cemetery wrote on Nov. 17, 1938 the following letter in response to an inquiry from Leila Hope Valentine Oberto: "Dear Mrs Oberto, I received your letter asking f
2 CONC or information on your ancestors. I am the Sec. Treas. of the Merrill Cemetery and all the information you are asking for is before the time of this church. It was built in 1857, the ground being given by Solomon Merrill, who with
2 CONC  his wife and family are the only Merrill's buried there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Solomon Merrill Born in 1814; Died Oct. 22, 1896 aged 82. His wife Maria Merrill born 1814 died in Dec. 29 1893 aged 79 yrs. Catherine Merrill wife of Damuel Dawe is buried here also. There were four daughters born to Solomon and 
2 CONC Maria Merrill.
2 CONT
2 CONT We tried to find the Family Bible back of the one in which Solomon Merrill's record in but so far we cannot trace it. But we have found out some information about the father of Solomon Merrill but we will have to go and confirm it
2 CONC  before I could tell it to you.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no one buried in the cemetery before 1862 or about that. There are around 300 buried there now and around 100 tombstones. Solomon Merrill gave this piece of land for the little church and cemetery. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I am dropping you this information so that you will know that your letter has been received and I will try to find out if I possibly can as much of the information which you require as soon as I can. As far as changes are concerne
2 CONC d you can wait until I have found out all I can and then just pay what you think it's worth. I might say that every year usually in August we have a memorial service in the little church and the money realized from this service ke
2 CONC eps up the grounds. The little church although only used when needed for a burial service is also kept up. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Yours sincerely, Charlton S. Grigg, Roseneath, Ont. P.S. Look for letter later..
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Solomon Merrill: Burial: Merrill Cemetery, Alnwick Township
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Solomon Merrill and Anna Lapp: Marriage: 04 July 1841, Cobourg, Ontario [<http://newsarch.rootsweb.com/th/read/CAN-ONT-NORTHUMBERLAND/2004-01/1073914918>]
