1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Thorpe's biographical sketch of Horace's son, Dr. Horace Wells:
2 CONT
2 CONT > ... Horace Wells, father of Dr. Horace Wells, married Miss Betsy Heath, of Warehouse Point, Connecticut, and soon removed to Hartford, Windsor County, Vermont, where the subject of this sketch was born January 21, 1815. This son
2 CONC  was the oldest of three children, the others being Charles Wells, M. D., who practiced at Manchester, New Hampshire, and Mary, wife of Captain John Cole, a sea captain who resided in Medway, Massachusetts. Mr. Wells, soon after t
2 CONC he birth of his first child, purchased a large farm at Westminster, Vermont, near Bellows Falls, on the Connecticut river. Here in a beautiful and romantic locality, and surrounded by every comfort his father could furnish, the ch
2 CONC ildhood of Horace was passed. The parents of young Wells were intelligent and, for that region, wealthy; and having the opportunity, gladly gave their children every advantage for moral and mental culture, sending them to the best
2 CONC  schools, and sparing no expense to make them useful members of society. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Thorpe, Burton Lee. ''History of Dental Surgery, Vol. III: Biographies of Pioneer American Dentists and Their Successors'', [https://books.google.com/books?id=RTdHAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA353&lpg=PA353 p. 353]. Fort Wayne, Ind.: National A
2 CONC rt Publishing Company.
