2 CONT Robert Burnham wrote in 2011:
2 CONT "Jehial Burnham b.1796 Thetford,VT and wife Amy Patterson abt 1800 had Charles 28Jul1819, Sarah 14Jan1821,  William Willard 27Sep1832, Nancy 14Jul1834, Burrell 23Jan1838"
2 CONT
2 CONT Burrell ''(Burnham,son of Jehiel)'' married Emily Pennock(1847-1919) 
2 CONT
2 CONT They lived in Yonge Mills, Ontario, Canada from 1819 until they died"
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==UNVERIFIED==
2 CONT * His place of birth
2 CONT * Where he went in his early years after 1790
2 CONT ** there is no record in census data for any Jehiel or Burrel  Burnam in VT
2 CONT *** was he in NY or Canada... In the [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000213240769846 split of his parents,] did he follow his mother (Mabel) ?
2 CONT
2 CONT * some genealogies have a son Charles (1819-1896)
2 CONT ** a record of note for Charles (possible match) is https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/181834315/charles-burnham   (1819-1896) in  Yonge Mills Cemetery, Yonge Mills, Leeds and Grenville United Counties, Ontario, Canada.
2 CONT ***perhaps Jehiel followed his mother Mabel to Canada?
2 CONT ** https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/119038599/burrel-burnham seems to have been Charles' son as they are both in the same cemetery
