1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Stillman Burnham: My records indicate Stillman's death as 15 Sep 1866.
2 CONT Stillman is shown in the 1860 Federal Census and the 1865 NYS Census Reports, so 1866 appears more likely than 1856. There is also an article by Frances D Broderick, a well regarded researcher from Lansingburgh NY, that gives deta
2 CONC ils about Stillman's funeral at the Trinity Episcopal Church in Troy NY. He was buried in their church yard, but no headstone has been found (the original church burned down on Dec 23, 1868)
2 CONT Roderick Burnham also shows Stillman's death in 1866
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Burnham c. 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Trinity belongs to the Episcopal Diocese of Albany. Trinity's History: Trinity Church was organized in January 1804. The building, designed by Philip Hooker, was completed in 1805. On December 25, 1868, a fire fueled by Christmas 
2 CONC greens destroyed the original church structure.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
