2 CONT <p>Notes</p><p>Moved to Granville, OH from MA in 1805 - among those who settled McKean, OH.</p><p>1850 United States Census</p><p>KELLY, Hugh 70 M Farmer 100 Ohio</p><p>Sarah 60 F "</p><p>Dennis 40 M Farmer "</p><p>Elluto 17 F "</
2 CONC p><p>Alford 15 M "</p><p>Sarah 13 F "</p><p>Elizabeth 4 F "</p><p>Sarah Spelman was born in East Granville, Mass. 29 Feb or 9 Mar 1784, anddied in Effingham C., Il., 13 April 1853; married in Granville, Mass., in Nov. (Granville c
2 CONC hurch Records), HUGH KELLEY, born in 1780 died in Baltimore, Ohio, 5 April 1854, They move to Granville, Ohio, with the settlers from Mass.,who went there in 1805, and later were among those who settled Mckean, Ohio. Hugh Kelley b
2 CONC uilt the second saw mill in Thattown in 1821-2, on Brushy Fork. He and his son, Hugh Denis Kelley, were contractors on the canal in 1838.</p>(this information reprinted from SPELMAN GENEALOGY page 202)
