1 NAME Erastus Frederick /Gaylord/
2 GIVN Erastus Frederick
2 SURN Gaylord
2 _MARNM Gaylord
2 NICK Erastus Frederick Gaylord
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 2 OCT 1795
2 PLAC East Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut, United States
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 JAN 1885
2 PLAC Cleveland, Cuyahoga, Ohio, United States
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Erastus had been a "country merchant" in Cornwall, Connecticut at the time of his Jan 1823 marriage to Lucetta Cleveland. Erastus bought the Madison, Madison Co., NY home and store of his brother-in-law Daniel Clev
2 CONC eland circa 1827 when Daniel and his family moved to Utica, NY. The Gaylords later moved to the "New Connecticut", and their Fall 1835 letters to Daniel Cleveland and his family persuaded Daniel to move his family to join the Gayl
2 CONC ords in their new location. The Gaylords lived on Seneca Street, Cleveland, Ohio at the time, and later had a large home on Woodland Avenue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Id#: 0112844 Name: Gaylord, Erastus F. Date: 1884 Source: Cemetery record; Cleveland Necrology File, Reel #029. Notes: 1797 - 1884. Lakeview Cemetery Cleveland, Ohio. The Pioneer Families of Cleveland 1796 - 1840. ByGERTRUDE VAN R
2 CONC ENSSELAER WIC KHAM: The name of Gaylord was a familiar one in Cleveland from the very early days when Capt. Allen Gaylord, his parents, and sisters came here from Connecticut..
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1833, two brothers of the same name and distantly related, also came from Connecticut to become citizens of this town. They were Erastus F. and Henry L. Gaylord, sons of Nehemiah and Esther Stevens Gaylord of Torringford, Conn.
2 CONC  Erastus had previously been a merchant of Cornwall, Conn., and was 38 years old when he came west. In 1832 he married Lucetta Cleveland, daughter of Gen. Erastus and Rebecca Berry Cleveland. She was born in Madison, N. Y., in 180
2 CONC 1, and, therefore, was 32 the year she reached Cleveland.. Her father held a commission as Brigadier-General in the war of 1812, and was in command of Sackett's Harbor and Oswego at different times. In civil life he was a judge of
2 CONC  common pleas court. Her grandfather, Lieut. Moses Cleveland, of Norwich, Conn., served in the Revolutionary army all through the eight years of that conflict. He was a cousin of Moses Cleveland, founder of this city..
2 CONT
2 CONT Erastus F. Gaylord opened a grocery and drug-store at 30 Superior street with A. F. Strickland as partner, and afterward with his brother, Henry Gaylord.In time the grocery department was eliminated, and "Gaylord's Drug Store," as
2 CONC  years passed, became a familiar landmark of the city. His son continued the business until his death in 1893, a period of 60 years.. Children of Erastus and Lucetta Cleveland Gaylord:. Sarah Berry Gaylord, m. Dr. John S. Newberry
2 CONC ... Henry Cleveland Gaylord, m. Catherine Hilliard. . Charles D. Gaylord, m. Josephine Scowden. Harriet R. Gaylord, m. 1st, George C. Hammond; 2nd, Dr. C. G. Smith..
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
