1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/59679978/person/46050296981 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 6 2018, 22:24:20 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Died age 51 years
2 CONT
2 CONT History and geography of Bradford County, Pennsylvania, 1615-1924 Chapter XVIII. Ulster Township Page 225
2 CONT
2 CONT Arriving in 1800 in Towanda, Bradford County, Pennsylvania - Reuben Hale was a native of Glastonbury, Connecticut.  He purchased the Grantier and several other properties on Towanda Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was very successful in his various investments and enterprises.  Mr Hale was a man of superior judgement and performed many public duties.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1810, he was appointed Towanda's first postmaster and was for several years a Justice of the Peace.  He died, 1825, aged 52 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife was Wealthy Tracy and their children: Eliza (Mrs Wm Patton) Nancy (Mrs Benj Spees) James Tracy Hale Elias Wellington Hale* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/137385920/reuben-hale Find A Grave Memorial] - [ht
