1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/59679978/person/46050296980 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 6 2018, 22:24:20 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Genealogical excerpts from the 1886 book "The History of the Susquehanna & Juniata Valleys" - page 466:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elias W. Hale was born in Glastonbury, Conn., April 18, 1775. He graduated at Yale College in 1794, and soon after began the study of law.....after completing his studies he removed to Lewistown and was admitted to practice in May
2 CONC , 1798. He died February 3, 1832 and is buried in St. Mark's Cemetery. Mr. Hale was married to Miss Jane Mulhollan, who survived him many years. Their children were George G., Reuben C., John M., Elias W., Mary and Caroline. Mary 
2 CONC became the wife of Gideon Welles, of Hartford, Conn., and Caroline married George D. Morgan of New York. Dr. Elias W. Hale is now living at Bellefonte.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source is book "Hale, House and Related Families"  by D. Jacobus.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Elias Hale was born at Glastonbury, Hartford County, CT on 11 April 1775, son of Gideon and Mary (White) Hale.  Married 26 Feb 1810 to Jane Mulhollan.  Died at Lewistown, Mifflin County, PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gideon Welles who was his son-in-law was Secretary of the Navy during the Civil War.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/55825529/elias-w-hale Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 Sm
2 CONC artCopy]: ''Aug 8 2020, 0:48:02 UTC''
