2 CONT MILITARY: Genealogical Records of
2 CONT Thomas Burnham, the Emigrant, and his Descendants
2 CONT Second Edition
2 CONT By Roderick H. Burnham
2 CONT Hartford,Conn.
2 CONT The Case, Lockwood & Brainard Co. Print  1884
2 CONT Page 209
2 CONT Edwin H. Burnham enlisted in the Fourth Regt. Conn. Vol. Infantry. After serving in the field about seven month, the regiment was ordered to garrison a fort at Arlington Heights, Va., where it was changed to the First Conn. Heavy 
2 CONC Artillery. They were at the siege of Yorktown, manning the heaviest batteries that were ever planted on this continent. At Malvern Hill they had fifteen guns planted upon a commanding position, that did good service. At the end of
2 CONC  three years he reenlisted and remained in the service till the 22nd of August, 1865, in all four years and three months.
