2 CONT
2 CONT AGE AT DEATH:  88 years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT OCCUPATION: A partner in the brass clockmaking firms of R. & J. B. Terry (1835-36), Terry, Downs, Burwell & Co. (1851-1852), and Terry, Downs & Co. (1853-1855).  He went bankrupt in 1855.  He went to Winsted for about ten years an
2 CONC d had charge of the movement shop of the Gilbert clock shops.  Thereafter, he went to farming. 
2 CONT
2 CONT RESIDENCE:  54 Middle Street,  "Middle n Pine" Street, Bristol, CT
2 CONT Two years after his son, Franklin Ensign Terry was born Raloh Terry and Ruth Lewis (Hubbell) Terry moved to a litter house on Preston Street, Forestville, CT 1847  They
2 CONT moved back to the Terry Homestead in 1850 (Three years after Anna Maria (Terry) Chase was born (1847) on Preton Street.
2 CONT
