1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT - According to,, and, Esther Gillet Terry was born on 9/19/1801.  and list her date of death as 3/27/1821.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Until now, little was known about Samuel Terry's eldest daughter.  Stephen Terry tells us that she was born in South Windsor or September 19, 1801.  There was no recorded date of death and apparently Esther did not marry.  It was
2 CONC  not known where Esther was buried. 
2 CONT A careful examination of cemetery records has uncovered Esther's burial site.  Old cemetery in Plymouth, behind the Plymouth Congregational Church, contains a stone marking behind Esther's grave.  The inscription is so well-worn t
2 CONC hat it is barely legible.  However, through the years of erosion and neglect, the following words can be discerned:
2 CONT
2 CONT Memory of
2 CONT ESTHER GILLET
2 CONT daughter of
2 CONT Samuel & Esther Terry
2 CONT Who was born Sept. 19, 1801
2 CONT and died March 27, 1821
2 CONT
2 CONT This is undoubtedly the grave of the Esther G. Terry in Stephen Terry's book.  Both the date of birth, as well as the names of her parents, confirm that.  The discovery of this stone answers many questions regarding what became of
2 CONC  Samuel's daughter, Esther G.  We now know that she died before her 20th birthday, several years before Samuel Terry  relocated from Plymouth to Bristol.  We also now know her date of death, as well as her final resting place.  Fi
2 CONC nally, we now know that the "G" in her name was deliberately spelled differently from her mother's maiden name, in order to avoid confusion.  Or, perhaps, the stone carver merely made an error when he carved the inscription." 
2 CONT
2 CONT PICTURES:
