2 CONT
2 CONT AGE AT DEATH:  56 years
2 CONT
2 CONT CHURCH MEMBERSHIP:  Admitted to the First Congregational Church, Bristol, CT on 3/19/1843 by Profession,.
2 CONT
2 CONT CEMETERY:  Milo Terry owns Lot 51 (the one in which he is buried) at Pine Grove Cemetery, Ansonia, CT, Sec. F.
2 CONT
2 CONT OTHER PROPERTY OWNED:
2 CONT On September 15, 1849, Grantor Samuel Terry of Bristol executed a quitclaim deed to Grantee Milo Terry of Bristol for one thousand thirty five dollars for land described as follows:
2 CONT “[A] certain piece of land situated in the 2nd tier of lots in said Bristol and is bounded as follows to wit:  South on the Highway, West on land of Mess’rs Terry & Andrews and land of Samuel S. Terry and on the River, North on la
2 CONC nd of Widow Lydia Pierce, East on land of Releasor containing eight acres more or less with the buildings thereon.”
2 CONT (Pine Street, Bristol, Connecticut 06010)(Lot # 1/1B)(Car Wash-Emerson Gillett Terry Home)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:  Samuel Terry to Milo Terry, Vol. 20, Page 546, September 15, 1849, Land Records, Bristol, Connecticut Town Clerk’s Office. (Pine Street, Bristol, Connecticut 06010)(Lot # 1/1B)(Car Wash-Emerson Gillett Terry Home)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT On September 15, 1849, Grantor Samuel Terry of Bristol executed a warrantee deed to Grantee Milo Terry of Bristol for one thousand thirty five dollars for land described as follows:
2 CONT “[A] certain piece of land situate in the 2nd tier of lots in Bristol aforesaid bounding South on the Highway, West on land of Terry & Andrews and land that I have this day deeded to Samuel S. Terry and on the River a part on each
2 CONC , North on land belonging to the Heir of Noble A. Pierce, Deceased and the Northeast corner of the premises hereby conveyed is a maple tree standing at the corner of the Pierce Lot and from thence running South in a direct line to
2 CONC  the Highway passing through the body of a Bevlton Ball tree about fourteen rods North of the Highway and contains eight acres more or less with the dwelling house and other buildings thereon standing.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:  Samuel Terry to Milo Terry, Vol. 22, Page 296, September 15, 1849, Land Records, Bristol, Connecticut Town Clerk’s Office.
2 CONT
2 CONT On September 15, 1849, Grantor Milo Terry of Bristol executed a warrantee deed to Grantee Samuel Terry of Bristol for five hundred dollars for land described as follows:
2 CONT “[T]he following described piece of land situated in the 2nd tier of lots in said Bristol and is bounded West on land of Samuel S. Terry and the River, North on land of Widow Lydia Pierce, East on land od the Grantee, South on the
2 CONC  Hartford Providence and Fishkill Rail Road containing five acres more or less.  Said Samuel Terry is to make and maintain all suitable and lawful fence between saind piece of land and said Rail Road.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:  Milo Terry to Samuel Terry, Vol. 22, Page 297, September 15, 1849, Land Records, Bristol, Connecticut Town Clerk’s Office.
2 CONT
2 CONT On May 31, 1851, Grantor Milo Terry of Derby executed a warrantee deed to Grantee Berkley D. Parsons of Derby for twelve hundred dollars for land described as follows:
2 CONT “[A] piece or parcel of land situated in the Town of Bristol in the County of Hartford and is bounded as follows to wit:  South on highway, West on land of Charles P. Clark and land of Samuel S. Terry, North on land of Hartford, P
2 CONC rovidence and Fishkill Rail Road Company and East on land of Samuel Terry containing two acres more or less with dwelling house and all other buildings thereon standing.  The said Parsons always maintaining the whole of the north 
2 CONC line of fence adjoining the Rail Road.”
2 CONT (Pine Street, Bristol, Connecticut 06010)(Lot 1/1B)(Car Wash-Emerson Gillett Terry Home)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:  Milo Terry to Berkley D. Parsons, Vol. 22, Page 488, May 31, 1851, Land Records, Bristol, Connecticut Town Clerk’s Office. (Pine Street, Bristol, Connecticut 06010)(Lot 1/1B)(Car Wash-Emerson Gillett Terry Home)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Clockmaking and Other Enterprises of Samuel Terry's Descendants
2 CONT Samuel Terry's sons William (1800-1822), Edward (1812-1866) and Milo Terry (1814-1870) were lesser known clockmakers, their working careers spent in the employ of other clockmaking firms."
2 CONT
2 CONT PICTURES:
2 CONT "Milo Terry Property (Pictures 1-4)":
2 CONT Corner lot in Ansonia CT, corner of So. Cliff Street, where it is believed one of the Terrys lived.  Terry Bradley Fletcher believes, as of 7/24/1997 that it was Milo Terry (born 3/9/1814 and died 12/6/1870) who owned this propert
2 CONC y.
2 CONT Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000185360628974label=@S66@
2 CONT Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000185360628962label=@S39@
