2 CONT Civil War Union Brevet Brigadier General. Served in the Civil War as Colonel and commander of the 8th Michigan Volunteer Cavalry. He was brevetted Brigadier General, US Volunteers on March 13, 1865 for "long, faithful and meritori
2 CONC ous services".
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisha Mix, Brig-General, Company F, 8th Michigan Infantry, and wife Emelia Mix, Allegan, Michigan 49010 (GPS N42°31.659, W085°51.767)
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisha Mix, from Manlius, Michigan was 44 years old when he enlisted on 11/1/1862 as a Captain. On 1/20/1863 he mustered into "F" Co. MI 8th Cavalry He was Mustered Out on 9/22/1865 at Nashville, TN
2 CONT
2 CONT He was listed as: POW 8/2/1864 Stoneman's Raid Exchanged 9/27/1864 (place not stated)
2 CONT
2 CONT Promotions: Major 3/2/1863 Lt Colonel 4/16/1864 Colonel 9/1/1864 Brig-General 3/13/1865 by Brevet
