2 CONC /56,1940 MERRILL, Glenn,Mrs.,76,1-Jan-82,(Luella M.),,1/1/82,1940 MERRILL, J.,,,20-Mar-09,C.,Lake MS,3/20/09,1960 MERRILL, Raymond,,90,31-Jul-93,J.,,7/31/93,1900 MERRILL, William,Mrs.,,6-Oct-16,(Lillian Craighead--should be Creigh
2 CONC ton, I now know--5/15/07--nms),Grand Rapids MI,10/6/16,1910 MERRILL Sr., Raymond,Mrs.,68,24-Jul-74,J.  (Mabel),,7/24/74,1970 http://www.rootsweb.com/~minemgs/nec_m_o.csv
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 Merill Albert 24 M W MI Fremont  from 1860 census index (heads of households only--check actualy census for others in household) http://www.rootsweb.com/~mialpena/Census/1860.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the 1860 actual census page, Grandpa Albert was in the household of Hylliard Broadwell.  I think this was a sawmill. Could this Broadwell fellow have been a friend of the family from New York?  I think both his grandp
2 CONC arents (Roger and Chloe) were from New York (it might be that Chloe was from Vermont--check back on this) 1 Broadwell Hylliard 48 M W NY Fremont  http://www.rootsweb.com/~mialpena/Census/1860.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Was he related to David, the one who did surveying and wrote about Alpena?  And were they both related to Ellen, Albert's first wife?   Oliver Robert B 21 M W NY Fremont  http://www.rootsweb.com/~mialpena/Census/1860.htm
2 CONT
