1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Major George Ogilvie Webster'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/49335417/george_ogilvie-webster
2 CONT
2 CONT Webster, George Ogilvie, July 29, 1843 born at Litchfield, Connecticut, son of Edwin B. and Anne E. M. Belden Webster; June 18, 1866 graduated from West Point (30/41) and appointed 2ndIt., 4th U.S Infantry Rgt. Nov. 15, 1867-May 6
2 CONC , 1875 regimental adjutant; November 25, 1873 1st Lt. December 16, 1880 married Mary V. Lane (March 9, 1859 born in Texas) at Ft. Sanders, Wyoming October 1, 1886-October 31, 1887 regimental adjutant; August 5, 1888 Captain July 1
2 CONC 897 commanding Company F; Santiago, Cuba; Philippine Insurrection; March 2, 1899 maj. Sept. 8, 1899 retired; October 10, 1899 died of fever contracted in the Philippines at Ft. Sheridan, Illinois Hospital and buried in Arlington, 
2 CONC Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT National Cemetery; Nov. 29, 1899 his widow Mary V. Webster applied for a pension (application #709350/certificate #485421) while living in District of Columbia; 1900 Mary was a patient in a Baltimore, Md. Hospital and the twins we
2 CONC re students at Lucy Cobb Institute at Athens, Ga. Children--twins: Charlotte B. and Florence P. Webster, Nov. 11, 1883 born at El Paso, Texas
