1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth/death information provided courtesy of Stephen's decendant, Linda Miesner.  Thank you
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen & Almira had one other known child not linked to them on findagrave. Daughter Myra E Brown, born Goshen, Litchfield, CT about 1846, married Henry E Janes on May 1, 1867 in Sharon, Conn. She died 1869 in Waterloo. Her husba
2 CONC nd was born Jan 10, 1840, died Dec 12, 1904 in Waterloo. His obit says he's buried in Elmwood cemetery, so she's probably there too.  The above information regarding their daughter, Myra, was provided courtesy of Find A Grave memb
2 CONC er Susan.  Thank you
2 CONT
2 CONT Although his obit allegedly records his burial in Elmwood Cemetery, his marker was found in Fairview Cemetery, Waterloo.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT BROWN, STEPHEN, farmer, Sec. 3 ; born in Litchfield Co., Conn., in 1816. Married Elmira Abbott in 1836 ; she was born in Berkshire Co., Mass., in 1817 ; they have five children living —Sarah, Hiram, Luther, Allen, Warren, and lost
2 CONC  one child—Myra. Came to this county in April, 1868, and settled on his present farm of 148 acres, valued at $40 per acre ; also carried on livery business at Waterloo six years of his residence in this county.
2 CONT {1878 History of Black Hawk County, Iowa}
2 CONT
