1 NAME Septerious Pitkin /House/
2 GIVN Septerious Pitkin
2 _MARNM House
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 23 JAN 1817
2 ADDR
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1887
1 OCCU Storekeeper
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Called Sam (Do you blame me?).  I was at the second
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilderness in 1864.  I was shot two days in a row.  Once through the nose and once in the leg.  I never had a limp. I always hated tomatoes because I laid in a tomato patch for three days with both Union and Confederate soldiers. 
2 CONC  All we had to eat or drink was those darned tomatoes.
2 CONT
2 CONT At one point, I had a small store with ? Hale in Hartford, CT but worked as a teamster (trucker) and farmer most of my life.
2 CONT
2 CONT All my brothers and sisters had the middle name Pitkin, which was my mother's maiden name.  There are several Pitkin relatives who were Governors of Connecticut.  There was also a Pitkin relative who was Governor of Colorado (Pitk
2 CONC in County is named after him.)
