1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Cornelius Savage, Jr.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/187892362/cornelius-savage Find A Grave Memorial ID # 187892362]
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of Cornelius Savage and Ellen Burnham, husband of Sarah E. Jones, whom he married on April 3, 1880 in Manhattan, New York, New York, and father of Cornelius Jones, Ella B. (married Miller) and Edward K. Savage.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1860, Cornelius Savage, aged 16, was living in Brooklyn, New York, in the home of his parents, Cornelius Savage, aged 50, and Ellen Savage, aged 41, with brother, Henry Savage, aged 8, servant, Ellen Degan, aged 20. His father 
2 CONC was shown to be a broker.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1900, Sarah E. Savage, aged 46, the daughter of English parents, was living on Hewes Street, Brooklyn, New York, with her husband, Cornelius Savage, to whom she had been married for twenty years. She was the mother of five chil
2 CONC dren, two of whom were living, Edward R. Savage, aged 9, and Ella Burnham Savage, aged 18. Her husband was shown to be silversmith.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1905, Cornelius Savage, aged 61, was living on Decatur Street in Brooklyn, New York, with his wife, Sarah Savage, aged 50. He was shown to be a silversmith.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary - Savage - Suddenly, on May 13, 1927, Cornelius Savage, beloved husband of Sarah E. Savage, in his 85th year. Funeral services will be held at his residence, 498C Jefferson Avenue, on Sunday, May 15 at 8 o'clock. Intermen
2 CONC t Centre Moriches, Long Island, Suffolk County, NY.
2 CONT
2 CONT (New York, New York City Marriage Records, 1829-1940, Reference ID cn2138, GS Film Number 1562357; 1900 US Federal Census; 1905 New York State Census; The Brooklyn Daily Eagle (Brooklyn, New York), 15 May 1927, Sunday, Page 20)
