2 PLAC Greenwood Cemetery Wilson, Niagara County, New York, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1842
2 ADDR
3 CITY Wilson
3 STAE NY
3 POST 14172
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lucy was born about 1806. She married Orange Stillman Post on 11 Aug 1825 in Dunham, Quebec, Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Links to parents are courtesy of Find-a-Grave Member # 49405556.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy died before Greenwood Cemetery was opened. Her stone is located in an area of Greenwood that was used for the reburial of individuals who were moved from the Nathaniel Davis Farm Cemetery, which was opened in 1846 on the east
2 CONC  side of Wilson-Cambria Road at the southern end of the Village of Wilson, and was closed in 1872, when construction began on a railroad line and depot that would utilize the same land. The cemetery's residents were removed to Gre
2 CONC enwood, or to another cemetery if the family so chose. Although Lucy's death predates the public opening of this cemetery as well, the location of her marker in Greenwood, in an area used for the relocation of individuals from the
2 CONC  Nathaniel Davis Farm Cemetery, suggests she was in that cemetery when it was closed.
