1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of Eliphalet Colt and Huldah Adams Colt
2 CONT
2 CONT Aged 80 years
2 CONT
2 CONT COLT, Wolcott (123Portland Sketches) d 1881 Was b. in Sandsfield, Mass, July 28, 1800. He came to Portland in 1822, and in March of that year, he articled p’t of lot 17, T. 5, farm now owned by his son Chandler. He m. Betsey, dau,
2 CONC  of Rev War Soldier Samuel Munson, in 1824. Mrs. C. was b. in Oneida county, N. Y., in April 1800. They lived upon their farm until 1856 when they removed to the Baptist parsonage on p’t of lot 26, T. 5, place now owned by Hiram B
2 CONC urton where Mrs. C. d. Oct. 7, that year. Mr. Colt. is still living, near North East, Pa. He was a bro. of Mrs. Nath. Reeder (No. 158) Mr. C. is an earnest member of the Protestant Methodist church; politically a republican. NOTES
2 CONC : Wolcott Colt died in 1881 in Conneaut, Ohio; remains were brought to Portland. and he was buried in Evergreen Cemetery beside his wife. Fredonia Censor 23 Feb. 1881.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=83950797
2 CONT ----
