2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/7a/94/d5/b5/53444849eca93cdf/1_large_original.jpg?hash=2a39a68f7488218e1387be226f4c36bef21a17b062f7060c4594bfd7dbc0b171.1794038399
2 FORM jpg
1 NOTE RFN: 28344
2 CONT Elijah is mentioned in his uncle, Phineas Drake's will in 1803, as
2 CONT receiving the sum of $33.34. The will was later set aside by the
2 CONT court.
2 CONT Elijah Drake had moved to the northern Vermont area before the birth
2 CONT of his children. Lyman was born in East Windsor, Vermont on the New
2 CONT Hampshire state line in 1796. Chauncey was born at New Haven about 10
2 CONT miles east of Lake Champlain in central Vermont in 1803. The date the
2 CONT family moved to Milton is not known but the War of 1812 had major
2 CONT battles on Lake Champlain and must have evoked great concern to the
2 CONT family.. Elijah fought in the Battle of Plattsburg, probably as a
2 CONT Vermont militiaman.
2 CONT Donald Craig
2 CONT EARLY HISTORY OF MILTON" from the Milton Story 1763 - 1963
2 CONT "The town of Milton is situated on the eastern shore of Lake Champlain
2 CONT in the northwestern corner of Chittenden County.
2 CONT The Charter of the town was granted on the 8th. day of June 1763 by
2 CONT Governor Benning Wentworth of Hew Hampshire. this grant of land was
2 CONT made to sixty-two grantees.---------The town was not settled as far as
2 CONT can be learned until the worst of the Revolutionary War was over,
2 CONT although settlements were encouraged in order to increase the land
2 CONT value.-----On the 5th. of August, 1786 the first lots divided--." Many
2 CONT of the first settlers were revolutionary war veterans. The first Town
2 CONT Hall was built in Checkerbury Green in 1803. It "was the pride of the
2 CONT town being quite large and fantastic. It was a square building with a
2 CONT huge chimney at the apex. It was built of the heavest of timbers and
2 CONT had massive double doors. The town meetings were held in this building
2 CONT until March 16, 1849."
2 CONT Family names link associations forgotten in history. After Elijah
2 CONT died, his widow Polly Tambling Drake married a man named Whittie, the
2 CONT same surname as that of their daughter-in-law, Lucinda Whittier, wife
2 CONT of Charles Stanford Drake. Elijah's brother, Phineas, named his first
2 CONT born son, Charles Cadman Drake. Christopher Cadman was the name of
2 CONT Polly's third husband. Chauncy Langdon Drake 's middle name appears to
2 CONT be much more remotely connected to the Drake family with the marriage
2 CONT of a distant cousin Polly Marie Drake in 1846 to Selah Hart Langdon
2 CONT or, more probible, a close association with one of the Langdon family
2 CONT members.
2 CONT Saw mills and grist mills were at the heart of the Milton economy.
2 CONT "The Battle of Plattsburg in 1815 [War of 1812] was remembered by many
2 CONT in Milton who watched the famous combat from a West Milton hill top.
2 CONT Cannon balls fired from ships were sometimes found on the Miltonshore.
2 CONT Fourteen of these War of 1812 soldiers are buried in the Milton
2 CONT cemetery."
2 CONT "The year 1816 was a period of hardship for Milton people. No seed was
2 CONT available for the spring planting. Everywhere there was a shortage of
2 CONT food. During the entire summer frosts were frequent and snow storms
2 CONT not unknown. All crops were greatly damaged and corn was ruined. Snow
2 CONT fell to a depth of 10 inches in June in some places. Planting and
2 CONT shivering were done together and the farmers who worked out their
2 CONT taxes on the county roads wore overcoats and mittens."
2 CONT A monument stands before the Town Hall. On it are inscribed the names
2 CONT of members of the Union Army including Chauncy and Orpha's two sons,
2 CONT Lyman and Leon Henry Drake.
