1 NOTE RFN: 3225
2 CONT Phineas Drake, his wife Sally, their son Phineas and their daughter
2 CONT and her husband, Tirzah and John Barstow all died of injuries suffered
2 CONT in the tornado of June 28, 1865.
2 CONT Ancestral File Number: 13L8-JMV
2 CONT Phineas and Sally Drake immigrated with their family from Genesee New
2 CONT York to Wisconsin about 1838-1839. Their daughter was born in 1836 in
2 CONT New York, and their son Burton's daughter Annette was born in New York
2 CONT in May 1837. They are found in the 1840 Wisconsin Census, so they had
2 CONT to have moved between May 1837 and 1840. Of the sons, Burton and Lyman
2 CONT Curtis remained in Wisconsin, while Charles Cadman, Horace and Albert
2 CONT moved on to California.
2 CONT 1850; Census Place: Kendall, Lafayette, Wisconsin; Roll: M432_1001;
2 CONT Page: 337; Image: 17.
2 CONT Burton Drake  35  b NY
2 CONT Aurett Drake   13  b NY  dau should be Annette
2 CONT Hannah Drake  9  b WI
2 CONT Ellen Drake      6  b  WI
2 CONT Hamilton Drake 2  b WI
2 CONT Phinehas Drake  65  b NY Father of Burton Drake
2 CONT Sally Drake        57  b NY Mother of Burton Drake
2 CONT Josiah Cushman  11 b ME
2 CONT Horace Drake     34 b NY  Brother of Burton Drake
2 CONT Phineas R. Drake 23 b NY Brother of Burton Drake
2 CONT 1860; Census Place: Franklin, Bad Ax, Wisconsin; Roll: M653_1399;
2 CONT Page: 230; Image: 233.
2 CONT Phineas Drak 75    should be Drake  b NY
2 CONT Sarah Drak 67  b NY
2 CONT Phineas Drak 33  b NY
2 CONT The Descendants of John Drake of Windsor, Connecticut
2 CONT Frank B. Gay
2 CONT Publishers: The Tuttle Company, Rutland Vermont
2 CONT pp 88.89
