1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Zerah was the second Rockwell brother to remove to western Pennsylvania from Berkshire County, Massachusetts. In western Massachusetts, along with his brothers, he assisted his father, Ephraim, in the manufacturing of rakes. In 18
2 CONC 16, in company with his younger brother, Bernard, he journeyed to Crawford County, Pennsylvania to investigate conditions and determine wither they deemed it advisable to remove to the Pennsylvania frontier area. They were well pl
2 CONC eased with what they found and purchased a tract of land on French Creek. They returned to Berkshire County and in the summer of 1818, together with numerous family members, returned to Crawford County, making the journey by means
2 CONC  of ox teams. It is not known for sure what route the Rockwells took in coming to Crawford Ckounty, but it would appear that they came across nothern Pennsylvania where part of the family (sons Allen and Abner and daughter, Sally)
2 CONC  decided to settle in Bradford County.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1825, the Zerah Rockwells joined the Presbyterian Church, in all probability the one at Gravel Run since the Cambridge Springs Presbyterian Church was not organized until April 22, 1852. Zerah Rockwell was one of the charter me
2 CONC mbers of the Cambridge Springs church and at its initial meeting he was elected elder along with Cyrus Mansfield.
