1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William A. McKnight, born 1800, in North Carolina.  In 1811, he came to Indiana, and in 1835 he removed to Clay County, Ill., where he bought land and improved it. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     He was one of the first to settle in that part of the county, and was a man of a great deal of energy and ability. He died in this county in the spring of 1862, from wounds received at the hands of robbers on the night of Octo
2 CONC ber 1, 1861, in Bible Grove Township.
2 CONT
2 CONT Excerpt from "History of Wayne and Clay Counties, Illinois 1884 " Note: Age:  62 y.
