1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Life sketch≤p>Keziah Hollister (Cooper). Keziah daughter of Isaac Hollister and Ruth Winchell was born in Olive, N.Y., Oct. 27, 1801; m. Samuel R. Cooper in 1827. He was born in Ulster Co., N.Y., Dec.18, 1806, and is a son of Char
2 CONC les Cooper and Elizabeth North. Both Keziah and Samuel removed from Ulster County to Tompkins County, New York with their parents, the former in 1813, and the latter in 1816. Here they were married in 1827. Samuel was a music-teac
2 CONC her and held some small offices. ≤/p>≤p>In 1869 they removed to Bourbon, Douglas Co., Ill., where they now reside in a vigorous old age. Heis a justice-of-the-peace. ≤/p>≤p>Children: ≤/p>≤p>-Hestira Cooper, b. March 29, 1829, in C
2 CONC aroline, Tompkins Co., N.Y.; m. 1st, James S. Mitch ell; 2d, Dr. Wilson; 3d, John William Steelman. ≤/p>≤p>-Martha Cooper, b. Aug. 22, 1 83 1 ; m. Sherman Beardsley, May 25, 1862.≤/p>≤p>-Mary E. Cooper, b. Dec. 12, 1834; m. Willia
2 CONC im E. Vickers, Aug. 5, 1863.≤/p>≤p>-Newton J. Cooper (AKA James Henry Conrad),b. March 31, 1838; m. Mary A. Gere, Aug. 5, 1863.≤/p>
2 CONT
