1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from the Penn State Library on Reuben Hale which has his papers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Reuben C. Hale attended Yale and was admitted to the Centre County, PA bar on 7 Aug. 1833. Practiced in Lewistown, PA and was a prominent lawyer in Mifflin County. Influential in state and regional law practice, business, politics
2 CONC , military affairs and Episcopal Church matters. In partnership with his brothers, bought a large amount of land in central PA and helped build the Tyrone and Clearfield Railroad. Married Sarah Jane Mills of West Hartford, CT on 1
2 CONC 2 May 1836.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/55825536/reuben-charles-hale Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 8 2020, 0:45:35 UTC''
