1 NAME Elias White /Hale/
2 GIVN Elias White
2 SURN Hale
2 _MARNM Hale
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Saint Marks Cemetery, Lewistown, Mifflin County, Pennsylvania, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 6 JUN 1824
1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 FEB 1892
1 TITL Dr
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Commemorative Biographical Record of Central Pennsylvania: Including the Counties of Centre, Clearfield, Jefferson and Clarion: Containing Biographical Sketches of Prominent and Representative Citizens, Etc. Chicag
2 CONC o: J. H. Beers, 1898, pages 78-79
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Elias W. Hale, the fourth child and last survivor of six children, read medicine under the direction of J. B. Ard, M. D., graduated from the University of Pennsylvania, and for a number of years practiced the profession at Lew
2 CONC istown, then removed to Reedsville, Penn., where he pursued the same calling.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the spring of 1864 he located in Bellefonte, at which place his practice was somewhat limited. In 1874, in connection with William P. Duncan & Co., he bought the old mill, and went into the milling business under the firm name 
2 CONC of Duncan, Hale & Co. Mr. Duncan retired in 1882, and the firm was changed to Gerberich, Hale & Co., Mr. Gerberich managing the business.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Hale was prominently connected with the Masonic fraternity, and he was well up in agricultural circles in the county and State. He always took a decided interest in agriculture, and invariably lent a hand to its advancement. H
2 CONC e was one of Bellefonte's shrewdest businessmen, and was an influential citizen from 1864 until the time of his death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was probably one of the largest property owners in Bellefonte, possessing, in addition to his real estate in the town, a number of fine farms in Centre and adjoining counties, and his wealth would foot up hundreds of thousands 
2 CONC of dollars. He was a partner in the Moshannon Banking Co., of Philipsburg, Penn.
2 CONT
2 CONT His death occurred in Mentone, Southern France, February 20, 1892, whither himself and family had gone the October before for his health.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Hale was twice married, his first wife being Miss Ellen Louise Steely, of the Kishacoquillas Valley, in Mifflin County, this State, by whom he had a son, Harry.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/55825530/elias-w
2 CONC hite-hale Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 8 2020, 0:48:02 UTC''
