1 TITL Judge
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elias was the son of Noah Lyman and Clarissa Granger.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Oct 9, 1828 in Bloomfield, VT he married Clarissa Crane Smith, daughter of Levi Smith and Caroline Matilda Cleveland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Shortly after their marriage they moved to Barford, Canada where he purchased a grist mill. By 1834 they had moved to Columbia, NH where they remained until April 1847 when they purchased their farm in Lemington, VT. They remained
2 CONC  there until their deaths. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elias, by accident, became blind four years before his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were Charles Channery, Russell, Cyrus Elias, Laura Lodema, Francis Amelia, Israel Watson, Marial Caroline, and Ann Eliza.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their first four children were born in Barford, Canada; the last four were born in Columbia, NH.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elias was Associate Judge of Essex County 1869-70; he was a Post Master, and held other town offices.
2 CONT
2 CONT Age: 75yrs 6mos 23dys
2 CONT
2 CONT Cause of Death: Heart Disease* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/162773833/elias-lyman Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 22 2021, 14:55:20 UTC''
