2 CONT
2 CONT He attended Williams College for 2 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served as a missionary to the Native Americans at the Congregational Church mission at Maumee, Ohio in the Old Northwest. He served from April 1831 to June 1833. He met his first wife, Sarah, at Maumee who was also serving as a
2 CONC  missionary. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a charter member of the Central Congregational Church in Madison, Ohio in 1830 and a founding member of the First Presbyterian Church, organized on October 13th, 1855 at Bowling Green, Ohio.
