1 NAME Francis Richardson /Peabody/
2 GIVN Francis Richardson
2 _MARNM Peabody
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 9 APR 1871
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 OCT 1950
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/11892315/francis_richardson-peabody
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of William R. Peabody and Mary E. Richardson. He married Ethel Webb Wright on 9-17-1903 in Akron, Ohio and they had 3-children. Francis was listed as the manager of a rubber shop.
2 CONT _____________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT THANKS TO BluMoKitty for the following information:
2 CONT
2 CONT Educated at Bridgton Academy and the Mass. Institute of Technology. Engaged in the rubber business at Akron, Ohio.
2 CONT
2 CONT married 17 Sept 1903 Akron, Summit Co., OH
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 3 children - John Gordon Wright 10 Jun 1905, Donald Webb 16 May 1907, David Thurston 7 Dec 1908
2 CONT
2 CONT ref: The Peabody Genealogy by Selim Hobart Peabody 1909; OH Death cert At his death he was a retired Mechanical Engineer. Cremation 30 Oct 1950 Highland Park Crematory Cleveland, OH
2 CONT _____________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT FROM THE AKRON CITY DIRECTORIES:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1905
2 CONT Francis R. Peabody, (Ethel W.), dept. supt. - Diamond Rubber Co., home - The Campania.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1910
2 CONT Francis R. Peabody, (Ethel W.), foreman - Goodyear Tire & Rubber Co., home - 104 Mayfield Ave.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1915
2 CONT Francis R. Peabody, (Ethel W.), agent - Acushnet Process Co., rubber refiners, Ohio Bldg., Phone Bell 2000 & People's Phone 1753, home - 28 Grand Ave.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1925
2 CONT Frances R. Peabody, (Ethel W.), with Brown Advertising Agency, home - 623 Minerva Place.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1930
2 CONT Francis R. Peabody, (Ethel W.), retail sales manager - H.G. Bogart Co., home - 623 Minerva Place.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also from the 1930 Directory:
2 CONT H.G. Bogart Co., (Harold G. Bogart), distributors - General Electric Refrigerators, 132 & 134 S. Howard St., Phone Main 1795.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1935
2 CONT Francis R. Peabody, (Ethel W.), salesman, home - 46 Kuder Ave.
2 CONT _____________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT Ashes buried in 1951.
