2 CONT William A. Merrill was a veteran of the Spanish-American War.  Grandpa told me that he spent his twenty-first birthday while a soldier in the war (recalled getting water from a well from a pretty girl on his birthday), so he was p
2 CONC robably in the army as early as 1897, although records of the Spanish-American War Veterans of Alpena, Michigan put his enlistment date as 26 Apr 1898.  Get this straightened out.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Alpena Evening News, Alpena, MI ~ Tuesday, 1 Aug 1899. Spanish American War- Company D, Third Infantry MEMBERSHIP IS FULL The Full Quota of Men Have Signed Company "D" Roll The numerous person who were anxious to join company 
2 CONC D," Third Infantry, but were unable to so will have to content themselves by waiting until a vacancy occurs in the ranks, and then take their chance with the many other applicants who were anxious but unable to get in the new comp
2 CONC any. At the meeting Friday evening, Captain W. D. Hitchcock received his full quota of men, and all have signed the company roll. About 50 of the men were members of Company B,: some having seen service in Cuba, and others being r
2 CONC ecruits, who were not given an opportunity to go to the front One man was a member of old Company "D," and the rest are men who have never belonged to any military organization. Captain Hitchcock says that he is proud of the perso
2 CONC nnel of the company, and expresses the opinion that it will be the best company the city has ever had. Only two of the men are under 21 years of age, and the average in height and weight is good. Captain Hitchcock will make a requ
2 CONC isition on the quartermaster-general for arms and equipments, and as soon as they are received drilling will be commenced...  Old members whose term of enlistment had expired and new members who signed the roll at the time of the 
2 CONC reorganization:  Wm. A. Merrill Arthur A. A. LeRoy (related to Martin? or was he a half-brother of William Albert's?) Corneilus O'Brien (is he related to Michael J. O'Brien, who was William Albert's uncle?) http://www.rootsweb.com
2 CONC /~mialpena/CoD.htm
