1 NAME Elizabeth /Daw/
2 GIVN Elizabeth
2 SURN Daw
2 _MARNM Daw
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 29 FEB 1861
2 ADDR
3 CITY Roseneath
3 STAE ON
3 CTRY Canada
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DAR, Daughters of the American Revolution - her D.A.R. number is 112266. 
2 CONT
2 CONT One letter says: Elizabeth lived there (Roseneath), till their father, Daniel Daw made a house for them in 1870, Henrietta, New York, he became a citizen, making the children also Americans.
2 CONT
2 CONT In a letter to Leila Hope Valentine Oberto, Elizabeth explains she is sending a photo of her [very large] house , in the shadow of Pikes Peak, in a beautiful part of the region on the Pikes Peak Ocean to Ocean Highway No. 24.  She
2 CONC  also said that she has been making her living  since her husband died in 1915, by renting out three of the four appartments in the very large house. (photo in my Merrill Photos)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Funeral folder: Mrs. Elizabeth Daw Nichols,  Born February 20, 1861, Ontario, CA. Departed February 17, 1940 Service held at the Trinity Methodist Church, Colorado Springs, CO.  Date February 20, 1940 at 2:00 PM Clergyman Dr.
2 CONC  Francis L. Geyer
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers Mr. Adelbert Livingston, Mr. Fred Shantz, Mr. Emory McKnight, Mr. Wm. O. Gaumer, Mr. Martin Drake, Mr. Wm. Schweikhardt.  Muscians Mrs. Lester Howard, Contralto, Mr. Bernard Vessey, Tennor, Mrs. Leonard Phelps, Accompa
2 CONC nist.
2 CONT
2 CONT Resting Place, Everygreen Cemetary, Colorado Springs, CO.
