0 @N6000000008307988920@ NOTE Savage
1 CONT ================
1 CONT THOMAS, Hartford, rem. to Windsor, after mid. age prob. and d. 1688, leav. Thomas, John, Samuel, William, and Richard (wh. all had fams.) beside four ds.   Descend. are very num.  
0 @N6000000008307989076@ NOTE m.  Mary Catlin
0 @N6000000008307959491@ NOTE m. Mary Caulwell
0 @N6000000008307989118@ NOTE m. Sarah Humpries
0 @N6000000008307989067@ NOTE Savage
1 CONT =============
1 CONT THOMAS, Windsor, s. of the preced. m. 4 Jan. 1677, Naomi, d. of Josiah Hull of the same, had Thomas, b. 16 Apr. 1678; John, 22 May 1681; and these bapt. at Hartford, Sarah, 7 Mar. 1686; Naomi, 3 June 1688; Abigail, 25 Mar. 1694; a
1 CONC nd Josiah, 6 Sept. 1696.  
0 @N6000000008307988749@ NOTE m.  Elizabeth Loomis
0 @N6000000008307989088@ NOTE m. Elizabeth Strong
0 @N6000000008307989094@ NOTE m. Milford Mulford
0 @N6000000008307989006@ NOTE m. Josiah Gaylord
0 @N6000000008307988986@ NOTE m. Jonah Williams
0 @N6000000000155784211@ NOTE All: Ancestry of Nathanial from chart from Minnie Witham,done from letterfrom Lois
1 CONT Dana of Hartland Vt. No documentation given.
1 CONT Found more info in Gen book on Thomas, the Emigrant. He was of Wethersfield,
1 CONT Conn. Graduated from Yale 1709. Was appointed surveyor to run line between
1 CONT Conn. & Mass.in 1714. Also did much more survey work re towns etc. Was often
1 CONT a Deputy from Wethersfield from 1722-33. and other political jobs.
0 @N6000000008307391830@ NOTE am note certain about parents - needs research
0 @N6000000003272293551@ NOTE [cornelius10anc.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [wolfe.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [ellis.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [error.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Joel noble resided in the northwest part of Granville, siz and a half miles from the center, on the road from West Granville village to Whitehall, NY
1 CONT
1 CONT From Debra Eddy's notes:
1 CONT They lived in Westfield, Massachusetts until 1797, moving to Granville, NY.  they lived 6 1/2 miles from the center of Granville.  Note--Westfiel, Massachusetts was originally in Hampshire Co, MA until the borders changed in 1812,
1 CONC  then it was in Hampden Co, Ma.  Only six of the thirteen children born to Joel and Naomi Noble survived to become adults.  Three of the babies died by age 6 months, the other four died before reaching their ninth birthday.  Resea
1 CONC rc:  "Descendants of Thomas Noble" by Boltwood---found at tLibrary of MI, Lansisng, MI, CS71.N72 genealogy), Pg 532, Joel Noble is Descendant #4606) "William Morton of Windsor, CT & some his descendant who are also Desc. of Thomas
1 CONC  Burnham" by  Ulysses Grant Morton & Addie LeDuc Morton, 1950 Birth of Joel Noble recorded in Latter Day Saints 1988 IGI of Massachusetts, #30,000-- listed three different times, tow as being in Wetfield, Hampden Co, MA, and the o
1 CONC ther at Granville, Hapden Co, MA.  Marraige recorded in Latter Day Saints IGI (1988) of Ma, #30,001.
